        "name": "USN-8160-1",
        "description": "It was discovered that MongoDB incorrectly handled length parameters in zlib-compressed network messages prior to authentication. An unauthenticated remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause MongoDB to allocate an oversized memory buffer, resulting in the exposure of sensitive information.",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2025-14847"
        ]
